<title>USA: U.S. DAP prices dip in quiet trade, ammonia flat.</title>
<headline>U.S. DAP prices dip in quiet trade, ammonia flat.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. cash diammonium phosphate drifted slightly lower Friday in quiet trade, and ammonia prices were steady.</p>
<p>&quot;It really quiet,&quot; one dealer said. &quot;The slow domestic market is softening prices somewhat.&quot;</p>
<p>The current pace of exports is enough to underpin the market, but a boost in the sales pace would be needed to increase prices, one dealer said.</p>
<p>&quot;Inventories don't seem too onerous, but we need more export sales to boost prices,&quot; a cash source said.</p>
<p>			     Dlrs/short ton     Chg from Wednesday</p>
<p>DAP central Fla	   177-180			dn 2</p>
<p>DAP central La Gulf     188-190			unc</p>
<p>Ammonia/La Gulf	     225			  unc</p>
